"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "3 John 1:6",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "64001006",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p>The church mentioned here was probably in Ephesus, where John was likely staying. Ephesus was an important port city in the province of Asia and was the fourth-largest city in the Roman Empire. It later became an important center for the Christian community (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Acts18:19-Acts19:41\">Acts 18:19–19:41</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/1Tim1:3\">1&nbsp;Timothy 1:3</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/1Pet1:1\">1&nbsp;Peter 1:1</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Rev2:1-Rev2:7\">Revelation 2:1–7</a>).</p>",
"associations": {
"passage": [
{
"start_ref": "64001006",
"start_ref_usfm": "3JN 1:6",
"end_ref": "64001006",
"end_ref_usfm": "3JN 1:6"
}
