{
"content_id": "14405",
"reference_id": 13573,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "3 John 1:12",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "64001012",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>Demetrius was the opposite of Diotrephes. Demetrius was a clear example of a person who knows the truth and lives according to it (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/3John1:3\">1:3</a>). His name appears at the end of the letter. This suggests that he was the person who carried John’s letter to Gaius (compare <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Col4:7-Col4:9\">Colossians 4:7–9</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/1Pet5:12\">1&nbsp;Peter 5:12</a>).</p></li><li><p><span><em>you know that our testimony is true</em></span>: John wanted to protect his honor as a trustworthy elder for these churches. He did not want Diotrephes or other false teachers to challenge or replace his leadership.</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
"passage": [
{
"start_ref": "64001012",
"start_ref_usfm": "3JN 1:12",
"end_ref": "64001012",
"end_ref_usfm": "3JN 1:12"
